using System.Collections.Generic;

// Hand-authored notes using Blizzard's quest, map and patch references.
public static class GuideDetails {
 static readonly Dictionary<string,string> extra=new Dictionary<string,string>{
  {"Blood Moor & Den of Evil", "ROUTE\r\nRogue Encampment → Blood Moor → Den of Evil. Look for the cave entrance outdoors; the Den has no waypoint.\r\n\r\nREWARD\r\nAkara grants one skill point and one free respecialization per difficulty after the quest. Save the respec until you need it.\r\n\r\nWATCH FOR\r\nFallen shamans can revive Fallen, so clear the shamans and check dead ends before leaving."},
  {"Cold Plains & Burial Grounds", "ROUTE\r\nTake the Cold Plains waypoint and explore the area for the Burial Grounds entrance. The Crypt and Mausoleum are optional side areas beside the cemetery.\r\n\r\nREWARD\r\nAfter Blood Raven dies, speak to Kashya for a Rogue mercenary. A new hire replaces your current mercenary.\r\n\r\nHELL FARM\r\nThe Mausoleum is a familiar undead-heavy Hell farming stop; check monster immunities and prioritize safety over clearing speed."},
  {"Stony Field & Dark Wood", "ROUTE\r\nStony Field → Underground Passage → Dark Wood. The passage has two levels; use level 1 to reach the Dark Wood. Return to Stony Field with Akara's translated scroll.\r\n\r\nREWARD\r\nRescuing Cain gives you a convenient identification service. Click his cage in Tristram and speak to him and Akara in town.\r\n\r\nOPTIONAL\r\nUnderground Passage level 2 became a level 85 area on Hell in patch 2.4."},
  {"Black Marsh & Forgotten Tower", "ROUTE\r\nUse the Black Marsh waypoint, find the tower and descend five cellar levels. The Countess is on the last level.\r\n\r\nTARGETS\r\nRepeat Countess runs for early runeword ingredients. On Hell she may also drop a Key of Terror. Her special rune table and ordinary monster drops have different limits; do not assume a particular rune is guaranteed.\r\n\r\nCAUTION\r\nTower packs can be dangerous in tight corridors, and resistances or immunities change with difficulty."},
  {"Monastery & Catacombs", "ROUTE\r\nOuter Cloister → Barracks → Jail → Inner Cloister → Cathedral → Catacombs. Take the Catacombs level 2 waypoint for repeat Andariel runs.\r\n\r\nREWARDS\r\nReturn the Malus to Charsi for one imbue. Defeat Andariel, then speak to Warriv to travel east. Check an item carefully before using the imbue reward.\r\n\r\nPREPARATION\r\nStock antidote potions, clear nearby packs, and leave room to move around Andariel."},
  {"Lut Gholein Sewers", "ROUTE\r\nEnter the sewers from Lut Gholein. Take the level 2 waypoint and find Radament on level 3.\r\n\r\nREWARD\r\nUse the Book of Skill to gain a skill point. Pick up the Horadric Scroll from the nearby chest and bring it to Cain to begin the staff investigation.\r\n\r\nWATCH FOR\r\nRadament can revive nearby undead; try to clear space and avoid fighting an entire room at once."},
  {"Halls, Maggot Lair & Viper Temple", "ROUTE\r\nDry Hills → Halls of the Dead level 3 for the Cube. Far Oasis → Maggot Lair level 3 for the Staff of Kings. Lost City → Valley of Snakes → Claw Viper Temple level 2 for the amulet.\r\n\r\nNEXT STEP\r\nPut the staff and amulet in the Cube and transmute them. Keep the finished Horadric Staff for the true tomb. The Halls level 2 has a waypoint; the Maggot Lair and Viper Temple do not.\r\n\r\nWARLOCK TIP\r\nNarrow Maggot Lair corridors can block your demon's path. Pull monsters into wider rooms where possible."},
  {"Arcane Sanctuary & Tombs", "ROUTE\r\nPalace Cellar → Arcane Sanctuary. Search its four branches for the Summoner and read the journal. The red portal takes you to the Canyon of the Magi; activate its waypoint.\r\n\r\nQUEST\r\nThe journal reveals the true tomb symbol. Find the matching entrance, use the staff in the Orifice, defeat Duriel, and speak to the person beyond him before returning to town.\r\n\r\nFARM\r\nOn Hell the Summoner may drop a Key of Hate. Duriel is dangerous at close range; thawing potions and cold resistance can help."},
  {"Spider Forest & Flayer Jungle", "ROUTE\r\nCollect Khalim's Eye from Spider Cavern in Spider Forest and his Brain from Flayer Dungeon level 3 in Flayer Jungle. Spider Cavern and Arachnid Lair are different entrances.\r\n\r\nSIDE QUEST\r\nFind the Gidbinn in Flayer Jungle, defeat the guardian, then return the blade to Ormus and speak with Asheara.\r\n\r\nFARM\r\nBlizzard raised Arachnid Lair and all three Swampy Pit levels to area level 85 on Hell in patch 2.4. Check for dangerous monster combinations."},
  {"Kurast Bazaar & Sewers", "ROUTE\r\nExplore Kurast Bazaar for the Ruined Temple and Lam Esen's Tome. Find the Kurast Sewers entrance in the Kurast area and descend to Khalim's Heart.\r\n\r\nREWARD\r\nReturn Lam Esen's Tome to Alkor for five attribute points per difficulty. Keep the Heart for the Khalim's Will transmutation.\r\n\r\nFARM\r\nThe Ruined Temple and Kurast Sewers level 1 are level 85 on Hell under Blizzard's patch 2.4 area changes."},
  {"Travincal & Durance of Hate", "ROUTE\r\nCollect Khalim's Eye, Brain, Heart and Flail, then transmute them in the Cube. Equip Khalim's Will and smash the Compelling Orb in Travincal. Take the Durance level 2 waypoint.\r\n\r\nQUEST\r\nDefeat the Council and Mephisto; enter the red portal beyond Mephisto to reach Act IV. D2R patch 2.4 made completing Khalim's Will a proper Act III requirement.\r\n\r\nFARM\r\nCouncil runs can yield gold and items; Mephisto is a boss target for gear. Watch Council Hydras and dangerous Durance packs."},
  {"Plains of Despair", "ROUTE\r\nPandemonium Fortress → Outer Steppes → Plains of Despair. Search the Plains for Izual; there is no waypoint in the Plains.\r\n\r\nREWARD\r\nAfter the fight, speak to the released spirit and then Tyrael for two skill points. Repeat this on each difficulty.\r\n\r\nPREPARATION\r\nExpect a long fight if your damage is low; leave room to retreat from surrounding packs."},
  {"River of Flame & Hellforge", "ROUTE\r\nCity of the Damned → River of Flame. Activate the River waypoint before searching for Hephasto and the Hellforge.\r\n\r\nQUEST REWARD\r\nTake Mephisto's Soulstone, defeat Hephasto, equip the Hellforge Hammer, place the stone on the forge and strike it. Expansion rune ranges: El–Amn in Normal, Sol–Um in Nightmare, Hel–Gul in Hell. The quest reward is once per character per difficulty.\r\n\r\nWATCH FOR\r\nThe river can contain dangerous mixed packs; do not rush into unexplored areas."},
  {"Chaos Sanctuary", "ROUTE\r\nStart at the River of Flame waypoint and follow the river to the sanctuary. Open all five seals and defeat the seal guardians to summon Diablo.\r\n\r\nFARM\r\nClear packs and seal bosses for experience and items; Diablo adds an act-boss kill at the end. Faster clear speed matters more than piling on magic find if your damage becomes too low.\r\n\r\nPREPARATION\r\nKeep fire and lightning resistance high, and watch for curses and enemy immunities."},
  {"Bloody Foothills & Frigid Highlands", "ROUTE\r\nHarrogath → Bloody Foothills → Frigid Highlands. Shenk is near the transition; the Frigid Highlands waypoint makes later runs shorter. Find and open all three soldier pens in the Highlands.\r\n\r\nREWARDS\r\nSpeak to Larzuk after Shenk for his socketing reward. Speak to Qual-Kehk after the rescue for Tal, Ral and Ort runes. Socket counts depend on the item; research the base first.\r\n\r\nFARM\r\nEldritch and Shenk can be combined into a quick repeat run, but do not stand under the falling projectiles after Shenk dies."},
  {"Frozen River & Halls of Vaught", "ROUTE\r\nCrystalline Passage → Frozen River for Anya. Bring Malah's potion back to Anya, return to town and speak with Malah and Anya. Anya's red portal leads toward Nihlathak.\r\n\r\nREWARDS\r\nUse Malah's Scroll of Resistance for +10 all resistances per difficulty. Anya also gives a class-specific item and offers personalization after Nihlathak.\r\n\r\nFARM\r\nHell Nihlathak may drop a Key of Destruction. His corpse explosions are a major danger. Activate waypoints deliberately; portal behavior depends on quest progression."},
  {"Arreat Summit & Worldstone Keep", "ROUTE\r\nAncients' Way → Arreat Summit. After defeating the Ancients, enter the Worldstone Keep and look for the level 2 waypoint, then continue to the Throne of Destruction.\r\n\r\nQUEST\r\nThe Ancients require level 20 / 40 / 60 for quest credit on Normal / Nightmare / Hell. Defeat Baal's waves and enter the chamber to fight Baal.\r\n\r\nFARM\r\nThe waves and Baal are useful repeat targets for experienced characters. Enemy combinations can vary, so adapt to immunities and retreat when needed."}
 };
 public static string For(string name){string value;return extra.TryGetValue(name,out value)?"\r\n\r\n"+value:"";}
}
